{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"mostlygeek.llama-swap","latestVersion":"272","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"copyright":"Copyright (c) 2024 Benson Wong","description":"Model swapping for llama.cpp","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/blob/HEAD/LICENSE.md","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"copyright":"Copyright (c) 2024 Benson Wong","description":"Model swapping for llama.cpp","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/blob/HEAD/LICENSE.md","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"llama-swap is a light weight, transparent proxy server that provides automatic model swapping to llama.cpp's server.","moniker":"llama-swap","name":"llama-swap","packageUrl":"https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap","publisher":"mostlygeek","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/issues","publisherUrl":"https://mostlygeek.com/","releaseNotes":"Three compatibility fixes and a couple of UI improvements.\nThis release is a collection of some UI improvements, compatibility\nenhancements and a bit of work to make content in this repo easy to import and\nreuse in the new https://llama-swap.ai website.\nThanks to everyone who filed detailed bugs and contributed changes. The\nquality of this project would not be where it is without the community.\n- 1249e7c changelog: make into package: makes changelog/ an importable Go package with Versions(), Latest() and Get() over the embedded per-release markdown so llama-swap.ai can display the release notes by @mostlygeek\n- PR #1315 ui: reduce ActivityTable render rate: throttles the Activity table to one render every 125 ms and skips redraws while the inflight panel is hidden, because live token/duration counters repainted on every update and burned CPU whenever several streams were active by @mostlygeek\n- PR #1318 UI: category and a capability badge for decision models: gives models declaring the decision capability their own sidebar/list category and a matching badge, since categories were derived from capabilities but decision models fell through with neither by @sousekd\n- PR #1319 internal/server: pass through 1xx interim responses in recorders: forwards 1xx statuses without recording them, because Expect: 100-continue (sent by curl for bodies over about 1 MiB) made the recorders latch onto the relayed 100 Continue and discard the real status, so upstream 400/500 errors arrived at the client as 200 by @mostlygeek\n- PR #1326 Remove metadata filtering to allow custom fields alongside capabilities: stops dropping architecture, capabilities, supported_parameters, context_length and context_window from user metadata when capabilities are set, since that metadata is nested under meta.llamaswap and cannot collide with the generated top-level fields by @mostlygeek\n- PR #1327 Add autoload=false support to /props endpoint: answers GET /props?autoload=false with 409 instead of loading a model that is not running (as llama-server's router mode does), so clients like llama.vscode that probe every listed model no longer load them one after another and evict the loaded model by @mostlygeek","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/releases/tag/v272","tags":["golang","llama","llamacpp","localllama","localllm","openai","openai-api","vllm"]}},"longDescription":"llama-swap is a light weight, transparent proxy server that provides automatic model swapping to llama.cpp's server.","moniker":"llama-swap","name":"llama-swap","packageUrl":"https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap","publisher":"mostlygeek","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/issues","publisherUrl":"https://mostlygeek.com/","releaseNotes":"Three compatibility fixes and a couple of UI improvements.\nThis release is a collection of some UI improvements, compatibility\nenhancements and a bit of work to make content in this repo easy to import and\nreuse in the new https://llama-swap.ai website.\nThanks to everyone who filed detailed bugs and contributed changes. The\nquality of this project would not be where it is without the community.\n- 1249e7c changelog: make into package: makes changelog/ an importable Go package with Versions(), Latest() and Get() over the embedded per-release markdown so llama-swap.ai can display the release notes by @mostlygeek\n- PR #1315 ui: reduce ActivityTable render rate: throttles the Activity table to one render every 125 ms and skips redraws while the inflight panel is hidden, because live token/duration counters repainted on every update and burned CPU whenever several streams were active by @mostlygeek\n- PR #1318 UI: category and a capability badge for decision models: gives models declaring the decision capability their own sidebar/list category and a matching badge, since categories were derived from capabilities but decision models fell through with neither by @sousekd\n- PR #1319 internal/server: pass through 1xx interim responses in recorders: forwards 1xx statuses without recording them, because Expect: 100-continue (sent by curl for bodies over about 1 MiB) made the recorders latch onto the relayed 100 Continue and discard the real status, so upstream 400/500 errors arrived at the client as 200 by @mostlygeek\n- PR #1326 Remove metadata filtering to allow custom fields alongside capabilities: stops dropping architecture, capabilities, supported_parameters, context_length and context_window from user metadata when capabilities are set, since that metadata is nested under meta.llamaswap and cannot collide with the generated top-level fields by @mostlygeek\n- PR #1327 Add autoload=false support to /props endpoint: answers GET /props?autoload=false with 409 instead of loading a model that is not running (as llama-server's router mode does), so clients like llama.vscode that probe every listed model no longer load them one after another and evict the loaded model by @mostlygeek","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/re